{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go","id":1342129,"title":"Infinite Macabre - To Darkly Go","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-18T11:03:25-07:00","id":1342129,"title":"Infinite Macabre - To Darkly Go","content":"I've been in a space opera mood lately (blame the <i>Picard</i> trailer) and I've been thinking about combining it with horror (blame <i>Outer Darkness</i>). Which leads me back around to <i>Infinite Macabre</i>, one of the sci-fi shards we did for 1e.<br /> <br /> There are really striking images in IM, including the Gates marked with pre-Atlantean runes, the Watchtowers waiting undiscovered on distant worlds, and vampire corsairs devouring their way through deep space. Chuck really gave space a haunted and sometimes grisly feel, and capturing that at a table would be awesome.<br /> <br /> I think if I were going to do an update/sequel, I'd want to add more factions (from the Sworn of the Void to the Jeffersonian Movement), explore the role of the God-Machine in the wider cosmos (we already know about the relay in Sirius), and get into the gritty of starships (both space combat and their dreaded Pandora Drives).<br /> <br /> I've written some notes and basic rules, but I'm still dialing in on an outline or a campaign pitch. The idea just won't let go...<br /> <br /> ...anybody else feeling this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T11:44:18-07:00","id":1342140,"title":"","content":"Hell yes. If it ends up needing writers, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T12:09:11-07:00","id":1342144,"title":"","content":"Definitely. The stuff I wrote on spirits of the Void Beyond and the cannibal dance of the planets and stars in Shunned by the Moon partly comes out of my general fascination with the intersection between horror and space as a creative canvas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T12:54:27-07:00","id":1342155,"title":"","content":"I would love to see more of this content. I am new to CofD so I don't know much about 1e, what book was Infinite Macabre in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T12:55:27-07:00","id":1342156,"title":"","content":"Infinite Macabre is definitely one of my favorite supplements for World Of Darkness, such that I have wanted to run a game involving an updated version. To hear interest in that is really exciting. Admittedly that\u2019s more for the scifi aspect than the horror, but more interest in this branch of the game is always great.<br /> <br /> I have (on and off) been planning out an interstellar Agency of Demons, each of them with their own unique methods of getting around space in ways that (they hope) the God-Machine wouldn\u2019t have a counter for. Stuff like using gadgets to allow faster than light travel for a spaceship, or creating stargate-like lambdas using only embeds, or suborning and moving particular Infrastructure. I even created a couple of tilts for planets that involve them having their own aetheric field (you can draw aether from the air but it\u2019s dangerous and slightly toxic) or no Essence at all (aether and essence usage is increased and gadgets don\u2019t work without aether fueling them). I also find the idea of an embeded gadgeteer to be a real boon for setting up a colony, even if they would need to be extra careful not to raise alarms within their tight-nit community.<br /> <br /> Beasts also strike me as beings who could get a lot of mileage from space travel, especially if they set of Chambers on separate planets and spaceships. Smugglers would give their eyeteeth (or probably someone else\u2019s) for access to that sort of network.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:18:24-07:00","id":1342165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342155#post1342155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see more of this content. I am new to CofD so I don't know much about 1e, what book was Infinite Macabre in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Infinite Macabre. It was one of the smaller supplements that came out a little after World of Darkness: Mirrors, along with Bleeding Edge, the cyberpunk setting hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:19:08-07:00","id":1342166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342155#post1342155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see more of this content. I am new to CofD so I don't know much about 1e, what book was Infinite Macabre in?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a standalone PDf product for Mirrors, since they couldn't fit it in the books but wanted to do it anyways. Same with Bleeding Edge for cyberpunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T13:28:30-07:00","id":1342169,"title":"","content":"Thank you both, I will have to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T14:35:24-07:00","id":1342186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go#post1342129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been in a space opera mood lately (blame the <i>Picard</i> trailer) and I've been thinking about combining it with horror (blame <i>Outer Darkness</i>). Which leads me back around to <i>Infinite Macabre</i>, one of the sci-fi shards we did for 1e.<br /> <br /> There are really striking images in IM, including the Gates marked with pre-Atlantean runes, the Watchtowers waiting undiscovered on distant worlds, and vampire corsairs devouring their way through deep space. Chuck really gave space a haunted and sometimes grisly feel, and capturing that at a table would be awesome.<br /> <br /> I think if I were going to do an update/sequel, I'd want to add more factions (from the Sworn of the Void to the Jeffersonian Movement), explore the role of the God-Machine in the wider cosmos (we already know about the relay in Sirius), and get into the gritty of starships (both space combat and their dreaded Pandora Drives).<br /> <br /> I've written some notes and basic rules, but I'm still dialing in on an outline or a campaign pitch. The idea just won't let go...<br /> <br /> ...anybody else feeling this?</div> </div> </div> </div>can I suggest combining it with the Fifth Sothic Turn for Mummy, and perhaps a BSG (2004) style religious pilgrimage in search for Starry Aaru in deep space?<br /> <br /> (I think I threw out there a while ago the idea of updating both scifi settings for 2e via future set Dark Eras, with Infinite Macabre being Mummy as described above, and Bleeding Edge being Demon, with the twist that the maintained alternate timelines by the GodMachine and subverted infrastructure allows for conflicting near futures)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-18-2019, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:05:45-07:00","id":1342193,"title":"","content":"Yes, please. I love space opera, and I'd love to write for a product like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:17:50-07:00","id":1342195,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm feeling it.<br /> <br /> DO EEEET.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:22:21-07:00","id":1342197,"title":"","content":"Definitely. A bunch of us were chatting about Mummies in space the other day on Discord and there's also [REDACTED], but that's still firmly under an NDA. Plus (tangentially) I think there's been some chatter about putting together a Scion: Space Opera book for the Nexus, so something is in the air. More stuff about space and set in space is an excellent thing. <br /> <br /> Yeah, if writers are needed, I too am all in for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T15:25:56-07:00","id":1342199,"title":"","content":"I would DEFINITELY buy it. I would love to buy whatever is made. I would immediately drop $100+ on a kickstarter for this.<br /> <br /> However, one thing that really bugged me about the original was the misuse of basic terminology and misunderstandings about the basic structure of space. The most jarring example of which was the bit where galaxies are claimed to be a generic term for star systems and planetary systems. (I think the confusion happened due to the technicality that galaxies could be considered star systems in the same way that a desert could be considered &quot;some sand&quot;; technically true but not really)<br /> <br /> For reference: a galaxy is a large blob (often a spiral actually) of hundreds of billions of stars (most of which have planets) separated from their neighboring galaxies by vast distances of empty space many times their own diameter. Our galaxy is called the Milky Way, our nearest neighboring galaxy is the Andromeda galaxy. Many works of fiction just refer to star systems and planetary systems as &quot;star systems&quot; or just &quot;systems&quot; and this is generally accepted.<br /> <br /> Most settings stick to a single galaxy as it has more than enough stars and is enormous enough to contain whatever the plot demands and leave the other galaxies out of reach. Except, of course, when they are used as a source of some sort of extra-galactic eldritch horror that can't be struck back against because they are too far away. A horror that sent their invaders to our galaxy countless eons ago, which have just now started arriving.<br /> <br /> The basic structure of space (as it matters for most space fiction): Stars are usually, but not always, orbited by planets. Stars sometimes orbit each other. Galaxies are composed of stars orbiting the center of the galaxy. The center of the galaxy has tons of stars and may be unsafe for colonization due to the sheer number of giant shortlived stars flooding the region with radiation. At the very center of a galaxy there is often a supermassive blackhole with a mass millions of times that of the Sun. Our galaxy has a supermassive blackhole at its center named Sagittarius A* (pronounced &quot;Sagittarius A-Star&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'm really not trying to be rude here. I really love the ideas. But those terminology and structure of space issues were just so jarring and really broke the mood for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-18-2019, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:53:02-07:00","id":1342225,"title":"","content":"This is something I've semi-jokingly noted, but something I think would be neat to see is that if there are any actual aliens humans run into (rather than simply having different splats be the 'aliens' of sorts), they'd see humans as the unspeakable horror of the universe. Why? Because humanity is so <i>changing</i> so gosh dang much. They can be turned into blood drinking vampires, their children can be born with their &quot;souls&quot; being a mishmash of human and spirits of rage, they can ascend into beings that play with the very fabric of reality, they can become fae wielding the power of their greaters, and so much more stranger and scarier things. Even their <i>dead</i> don't stop changing into strange and mutually exclusive things. Further, while humans aren't the only things on earth that can do this on earth, they tend to be the ones who get changed the most while staying visually the same the most.<br /> <br /> Humans may be scared of what's in outer space, but considering what any one human being could become under any number of circumstances, humanity may be the <i>real</i> horror in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T16:56:48-07:00","id":1342226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342197#post1342197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely. A bunch of us were chatting about Mummies in space the other day on Discord and there's also [REDACTED], but that's still firmly under an NDA. Plus (tangentially) I think there's been some chatter about putting together a Scion: Space Opera book for the Nexus, so something is in the air. More stuff about space and set in space is an excellent thing. <br /> <br /> Yeah, if writers are needed, I too am all in for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually sounds pretty cool. I mean the Mummies would be like &quot;seeya judge, I'm peacing out!&quot; As they take a ship to go somewhere else. <br /> <br /> I love Mirrors, and its pdf supplements, so to see this idea is really cool. <br /> <br /> Also to imagine that after everying bad in CoD we still manage to go into space. Its very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T17:41:24-07:00","id":1342233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342199#post1342199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would DEFINITELY buy it. I would love to buy whatever is made. I would immediately drop $100+ on a kickstarter for this.<br /> <br /> However, one thing that really bugged me about the original was the misuse of basic terminology and misunderstandings about the basic structure of space. The most jarring example of which was the bit where galaxies are claimed to be a generic term for star systems and planetary systems. (I think the confusion happened due to the technicality that galaxies could be considered star systems in the same way that a desert could be considered &quot;some sand&quot;; technically true but not really)<br /> <br /> For reference: a galaxy is a large blob (often a spiral actually) of hundreds of billions of stars (most of which have planets) separated from their neighboring galaxies by vast distances of empty space many times their own diameter. Our galaxy is called the Milky Way, our nearest neighboring galaxy is the Andromeda galaxy. Many works of fiction just refer to star systems and planetary systems as &quot;star systems&quot; or just &quot;systems&quot; and this is generally accepted.<br /> <br /> Most settings stick to a single galaxy as it has more than enough stars and is enormous enough to contain whatever the plot demands and leave the other galaxies out of reach. Except, of course, when they are used as a source of some sort of extra-galactic eldritch horror that can't be struck back against because they are too far away. A horror that sent their invaders to our galaxy countless eons ago, which have just now started arriving.<br /> <br /> The basic structure of space (as it matters for most space fiction): Stars are usually, but not always, orbited by planets. Stars sometimes orbit each other. Galaxies are composed of stars orbiting the center of the galaxy. The center of the galaxy has tons of stars and may be unsafe for colonization due to the sheer number of giant shortlived stars flooding the region with radiation. At the very center of a galaxy there is often a supermassive blackhole with a mass millions of times that of the Sun. Our galaxy has a supermassive blackhole at its center named Sagittarius A* (pronounced &quot;Sagittarius A-Star&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'm really not trying to be rude here. I really love the ideas. But those terminology and structure of space issues were just so jarring and really broke the mood for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. It's an easy fix and builds on the secretly-science-fiction theme of the CofD.<br /> <br /> Side note: Sagittarius A* is an awesome &quot;forbidden zone&quot;, because the theory is that the existence of it allowed the Milky Way to exist in the first place; a gas cloud undergoing collapse formed it, and the newfound gravity caused a chain reaction in the orbiting nebulae that formed new stars. This, combined with the fact older stuff is at the center, can you say &quot;xenophobic ancient black hole worshiping civilization with eldritch interests&quot;?<br /> <br /> On that note, I've been reading old Hero System stuff and they actually fused science fiction with magical horror brilliantly, and in a way that's an excellent Infinite Macabre antagonist; the Church of the Infinite Dark, which is not actually a religion so much as a <i>classification </i>for what happens when scientists make contact with eldritch horrors from below the universe (the Kings of Edom, to be precise) and become fanatical space pirates who fly haunted Event Horizon-style ships. Also, the Elder Worm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T18:04:22-07:00","id":1342239,"title":"","content":"I'm intrigued, and would definitely welcome such a product. Dead Space was one of my favorite video games, and there is so few IP out there as space horror. A Chronicles of Darkness focused not only in the future but in the void of space is such a rich idea I'm surprised it hasn't been more pushed (Yes I know Warhammer but they are a whole other thing focused more on wars and such). Either way, love the idea and would so want in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T18:11:12-07:00","id":1342240,"title":"","content":"Well, let me know when you want to make a Kickstarter of this. I'll put some money aside to help make it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T18:17:10-07:00","id":1342243,"title":"","content":"Some cool stuff to get people in the mood for space:<br /> <br /> -Here is a cool image of our galaxy from nasa:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/sites/default/files/images/620057main_milkyway_full.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/mission_pages/sunearth/news/gallery/galaxy-location.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.nasa.gov/mission_pages/s...-location.html</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> -Also here is a famous to-scale diagram of just the solar system which I like to revisit periodically to be reminded how frustratingly, terrifyingly big and empty space is:<br /> <a href=\"http://joshworth.com/dev/pixelspace/pixelspace_solarsystem.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://joshworth.com/dev/pixelspace/...larsystem.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-18-2019, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T20:03:46-07:00","id":1342262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342155#post1342155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see more of this content. I am new to CofD so I don't know much about 1e, what book was Infinite Macabre in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The original supplement, containing a series of variant rule systems and alternate settings, was <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/82477?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=OPPforums\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: Mirrors</a>.<br /> <br /> Mini-PDFs of extra material which couldn't fit in Mirrors were <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/87936?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=OPPforum\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Bleeding Edge</a> (two different takes on the cyberpunk genre), and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/87937?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=OPPforum\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Infinite Macabre</a> (space opera).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T21:13:46-07:00","id":1342273,"title":"","content":"I'm 90% certain Infinite Macabre was, if not the first, then the second PDF I ever actually bought for CofD, and it got stuck in my brain for a long time. I've thought a lot about the <i>Orphans of the Sky </i>meets World of Darkness game I'm pretty sure I'll never get a chance to run. Something about vampires and not knowing what a sun is...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T21:32:34-07:00","id":1342275,"title":"","content":"That said, I really, <i>really</i> hope that they don\u2019t suggest the Star Crossed Lovers aspect with Changeling again, where the Gentry and Changeling genuinely were in love. It felt very... tone deaf when you look at the source material. I get that the suggestion was meant as a deconstruction alongside making the Gentry alien beings, and how Changelings could be making a rebellion against them... but \u201ca measure of planetary romance by falling in forbidden love with her Keeper\u201d, and comparing it to Romeo and Juliet, still feels squicky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T23:46:10-07:00","id":1342287,"title":"","content":"I doubt that'll happen again.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say there won't be any star-crossing, particularly if I get to vent five years of headspace on the subject.<br /> <br /> The fault in our stars is a weird and terrifying place to be indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:30:49-07:00","id":1342293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342287#post1342287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt that'll happen again.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say there won't be any star-crossing, particularly if I get to vent five years of headspace on the subject.<br /> <br /> The fault in our stars is a weird and terrifying place to be indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did that make me think of a Fawlty Towers scenario, but it\u2019s Fawlty Stars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T00:36:29-07:00","id":1342296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342293#post1342293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why did that make me think of a Fawlty Towers scenario, but it\u2019s Fawlty Stars?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea, I have no clue what you're talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T01:06:06-07:00","id":1342304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342296#post1342296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea, I have no clue what you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a British comedy about a terribly run hotel, the owner being Basil Fawlty. Throw in the wordplay, and that\u2019s the basic premise. Now escalate it to there being stars with faults in them, attempts to contain them or exploit them going awry...<br /> <br /> Equal opportunity for cosmic horror and dark comedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T02:18:31-07:00","id":1342311,"title":"","content":"I am 110% behind this! Infinite Macabre is the thing that pulled me into CofD in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T07:57:11-07:00","id":1342348,"title":"","content":"Make it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T08:27:02-07:00","id":1342350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342304#post1342304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s a British comedy about a terribly run hotel, the owner being Basil Fawlty. Throw in the wordplay, and that\u2019s the basic premise. Now escalate it to there being stars with faults in them, attempts to contain them or exploit them going awry...<br /> <br /> Equal opportunity for cosmic horror and dark comedy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wonder what a cosmic hearing aid is like.<br /> <br /> And I just realized how pertinent my Snarky Nerd Deviant is to this:<br /> <br /> &quot;I discovered the real version of the Force. Good news is, the dark side doesn't corrupt you, or if it does, you become more you more than anything. Bad news is, there is no light side. There is no peace, there is only passion.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T09:46:18-07:00","id":1342362,"title":"","content":"So, when is pitch season again? Alternately, is there a generic area in the Storyteller\u2019s Vault for things like this?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d buy it, definitely. Especially if there were rules for creating aliens that were roughly on the order of human power (maybe a set of merits representing nonhuman body structures and mindsets) so you can do the Federation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T19:41:31-07:00","id":1343079,"title":"","content":"Something that Infinite Macabre vaguely alluded to was the idea of spaceships matching supernatural splats, like Vampire ships having a gothic cathedral appearance. While this initially inspired me to try and make time ships based on each splat (Vampire ships used blood to calculate where a person was and could travel to those points, for example), this also made me wonder what each splat would be like in spaceship form. If we were to get an updated/expanded version of Infinite Macabre, I\u2019d like to see this kind of concept explored.<br /> <br /> Also, Angel spaceships that Fall sounds like an awesome concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T06:49:58-07:00","id":1343154,"title":"","content":"I'd personally <i>love </i>to see Infinite Macabre get an update, especially since there's now 4 more major splat templates to play with (Mummies, Demons, Beasts, and Deviants). It'd be fun for those of us who ever decide we want to take our games to the stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11208-thehailstormer","name":"TheHailStormer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11208_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:14:57-07:00","id":1343163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1343079#post1343079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that Infinite Macabre vaguely alluded to was the idea of spaceships matching supernatural splats, like Vampire ships having a gothic cathedral appearance. While this initially inspired me to try and make time ships based on each splat (Vampire ships used blood to calculate where a person was and could travel to those points, for example), this also made me wonder what each splat would be like in spaceship form. If we were to get an updated/expanded version of Infinite Macabre, I\u2019d like to see this kind of concept explored.<br /> <br /> Also, Angel spaceships that Fall sounds like an awesome concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leading off what TheHailStormer said, I wonder what thematics the new gamelines would have. I can imagine Unchained have a more hardscrabble version of whatever loyalist angels have (or that angels have crystalline and delicate ships while demons have obviously organic ones, to tie into the whole Order vs Chaos thing), Arisen have no distinction between sorcery and tech on their ships (and Iremites in general probably don't see a difference), and Beasts snatch up what they can and add spikes and glowing red panels to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T06:48:28-07:00","id":1343398,"title":"","content":"Though, can I say? No Always Chaotic Evil among species native to the mortal coil. There can be, and should be, tyrannical empires, but any sentient race has virtues and faults.<br /> <br /> Part of this is boredom and frustration with &quot;orcs&quot; as a concept, but mostly because we have innately hostile supernatural beings already, an alien should come off as a true stranger - which is to say, not hostile, but thinking in terms you aren't familiar with and interaction is fraught because you don't know if you're going to make them hostile when you didn't need it to be.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that there can't be world-devouring swarms of monsters, but I'd make them explicitly mindless. There's a thread on RPGnet that has a thematic idea for this, the Apoc drone fleet; they are actually an autonomous self-constructing exploration probe designed for gifting first contact to life as the epitaph of their long-gone creators, but sadly their creators evolved on a gas giant and literally did not conceive of rocky worlds bearing life; thus, when the Apoc come to a rocky world, they start strip-mining the &quot;asteroid&quot; to build more Apoc or terraforming it into a gas giant for life to flourish in, and if attacked they assume they've encountered hostile hyperspace life and engage defensive protocols.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Apoc is a berserk, heavily armed gravestone. Very fitting for a universe where warp travel involves the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T14:01:52-07:00","id":1343493,"title":"","content":"You could have something that is alive and intelligent but nearly entirely hostile.<br /> <br /> Imagine a hive mind organism that evolved from an ecosystem spanning colony of creatures; a continent spanning supercolony of perhaps ant-like animals. The colony itself persisted and the species evolved increasingly complex interactions over millions of years of their one colony dominating the world. Eventually evolving specialized individuals which store information allowing it to learn. Eventually this colony mind achieved sapience, though it took hours or days to think a thought as all of the little alien ants that form its body and mind move around. This colony mind was a huge advantage to the species further cementing their domination of their continent.<br /> <br /> Over another million years it evolved and consolidated, instead of operating as just the results of the interactions of ants, the memory ants evolved into huge immobile masses of brain at the hearts of nests. Living cables ants evolved to connect the nests for faster networking. Eventually it developed technology, which eventually lead to it integrating computers and radio into its colony, speeding up its thought processes greatly as brains hundreds of miles away can be consulted instantly instead of taking several minutes for the signal to move along the cable ants. It eventually colonized the rest of its world's continents. Finally, it developed space travel and encountered something it had only speculated might exist, and was ill-prepared to understand: other intelligent beings.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is a massive hive mind that doesn't have proper Theory of Mind and is terrified of other intelligence because it lacks any natural ability to guess what a sapient being might do. Its lived millions of years, though it has forgotten most of that as it didn't have very good memory until recently (that's what caused the explosion of tech development, an evolutionary breakthrough in long term memory).<br /> <br /> It doesn't have empathy or sympathy or any natural ability to relate to another thinking creature at all. Language is a foreign concept to it. War is a foreign concept to it. Trade is a foreign concept to it. Kindness, hatred, compassion, sharing, friendship, and rivalry are all foreign concepts to it. It barely grasps the concept of individually sapient creatures, a concept that shocked and disgusted it when it first discovered them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: An idea for something that might be playable:<br /> <br /> Imagine a species of solitary predators that achieved sapience in an arms race with a prey species that was also achieving sapience. As minimally social creatures they never developed civilization while the prey species did and so they mostly ceased to prey upon them as their fangs, claws, and stone tools aren't really a match for even an iron age civilization. Eventually the civilization realizes that those creatures that occasionally eat them are actually intelligent and attempt to integrate and use them in their societies them (probably as slaves at first based if our iron age civilizations are anything to go on).<br /> <br /> Eventually the civilization advances and reaches space and brings their tamed predators with them. The galactic stage now has an entire species of antisocial loners that have none of the things that social species have, no empathy, sympathy, compassion, kindness, morality, or anything like that. They would never have formed a civilization on their own but instead got brought to space by a species they evolved to eat. They understand the rules of society and don't just kill people for the sake of killing or whatever, but usually end up as assassins or mercenaries or just lone freighter pilots or late night clerks because they are naturally territorial and don't bond or form groups with others easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 10-24-2019, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T21:20:33-07:00","id":1343532,"title":"","content":"Man, I've run a gritty fantasy Mars setting - corporations rule orbit, human employees on the surface under their rule are practically prisoners with jobs, the wilderness of Mars like Heinlein or Bradbury's vision of the world - using ChroD stuff, that was a heck of a good time. Primarily Changeling and Geist (a dead world of which humanity has dreamed for eons). I might still have some notes sitting around.<br /> <br /> I've also done Geist as a space opera - the PCs died and when they woke from their Bargains, found themselves on the deck of a mysterious spacecraft, shades of the Flying Dutchman in space kind of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T21:23:24-07:00","id":1343533,"title":"","content":"found the old Mars pitch<br /> <br /> The first Mars colonies were established in the 2040s, and others soon followed. Mining operations on asteroids and Mars became big business and the corporate concerns that oversaw them bloated under their weight. Earth started to run out of clean water and food about ten years later. Decades of political squabbling over the truth of any potential problems left a world devoid of solutions to those problems, and riots began. The same story of ages past played out before \u2013 war burst out, colonies stopped imports and exports, and people stranded in the reaches of space began to die.<br /> <br /> The Martians didn't.<br /> <br /> They buckled down and weathered the vanishing support with fortitude and perseverance born out of their frontier ancestors and they lived \u2013 thrived, you might even say \u2013 in the cold, red wastes. Gangs became tribes, and tribes warred among each other over dwindling resources, renewable energy materiel, and found ways to integrate ever stranger things into their bodies, to better stave off the terrible climate. A century passed, and signals from Earth came again. The companies that put the ancestors on the red dust came back and claimed ownership over the Martians and their tools, and the Martian propensity for war turned up.<br /> <br /> That didn't work out too well; the invaders held the ultimate high ground, and even with all their cybernetics and emancipated robots and reborn machinery, the Martians did not win the day. The companies came down and reprogrammed what they could, fixed what they couldn't, extracted hefty fees from the rebels, and locked down the colonies. Now mines and work camps are little more than prisons, and they make them more like that every day, shipping in new meat from Earth to grind up in the mines, ignoring the tribes living squalid existences in the dust.<br /> <br /> These corporate concerns sit in orbit in their glittering homes with terraforming implements and gases all sitting and waiting for the button to be pressed to turn Mars into a new Earth, but they don't because the bottom line says that would lose them more money than it would save. They set lights out and exercise periods and uniform requirements for employees on the ground and implement their decisions through ruthless robotic stand-ins. It's 2150 and it's same-shit, different-day.<br /> <br /> You've either just shipped in or you're in the habs already; your next place of living is Nova-Mine Habitat Facility 457-Bravo-Hotel-Papa at the edge of Argyre Basin, or, as the residents know it, Hotel California.<br /> <br /> Maybe you died. You suffocated in the thin air, you got pulped by a mining machine, you were the last survivor of a Martian raid or a casualty of war. Whatever happened, you got back up, you just had something else in your brain that tells you to kill, to fight back, to let the Martian dead find their rest and their exaltation in war.<br /> <br /> Maybe you went somewhere you shouldn't have. You found yourself in a winding canyon during exploratory EVA, your ship crashed someplace it couldn't have, your adulthood ritual among the tribe went wrong, and you found yourself in some other Mars, someplace with canals and angry red weeds and Martian cabbage and you took water with strange things in the depths of the caverns or hiding among the sharp-edged ruins and you know that Mars is still out there, and it wants to be set free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T21:35:22-07:00","id":1343536,"title":"","content":"and found my Geist pitch<br /> <br /> Things did not go well on your first spacewalk. A faulty stitch in the suit tore, and you were stranded on the far side of the hab module. You tried to make the walk back, but you lost consciousness within sight of the hatch. An eye the size of a planet asked that you return to life, bearing its message.<br /> <br /> You were catapulted into space when the impossible happened \u2013 a debris collision. You burned to death in the empty void before you suffocated. Humans can live up to a minute without air, but exposed to space, your own body coupled with the light from a nearby star, with nowhere to diffuse heat, will cook you from the inside-out. As your brain bloated under the strain of the temperature rising in your blood, something red and older than the stars managed to find you.<br /> <br /> You awoke on the deck of a ship, the dedication plaque old and stained, with a thousand or more names etched into the wall in chalk, blood, and knife blade. It has known many names \u2013 Caleuche, Flying Dutchman, the waku wairua \u2013 and has sailed every sea. The stars are just one more ocean, and it has seen a million dead worlds. For better or worse, you are its crew now. Set the dead to rest, and search for wonder among the stars, but be warned. It's not for the living \u2013 or the timid.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:01:57-07:00","id":1343842,"title":"","content":"I pretty much love all of the stuff that came out of the guides - many of the rules widgets became part of CoD core rules. They're brilliant and should be re-imagined for CoD 2 with more details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T20:29:25-08:00","id":1350573,"title":"","content":"Actually, bumping this because of Death Stranding.<br /> <br /> The tech there is an excellent visual thematic to what I think Sekhem-based technology is like when the Arisen decide to make their Tombs space-capable. It <i>looks </i>like mundane, if highly advanced, tech, and on some level it is; ultimately human civilization directs and collects Sekhem, as do human crafts, up to and including information technology. However, even a cursory examination of how it works shows that it messes with parts of the universe that really shouldn't be able to be messed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:31:58-08:00","id":1351341,"title":"","content":"I'm on a kick.<br /> <br /> I think what we really need, along with splat-based ships, is alternate hyperdrives.<br /> <br /> Most people probably use the Void and the Gates to it; it's relatively safe, as most ghosts at worse will stow away to get back to a living world to resolve their anchors, and the Underworld is already partly a sea that can be conceptualized and navigated as such. But sometimes, you want speed, or an unexpected route, or flexibility in where you enter/exit hyperspace.<br /> <br /> More importantly, you want it more than you want a safe trip. Which is where you get a drive that dives into the Shadow to negotiate with the void-spirits for use of perspective-based wormholes, or flickers into the Hedge to take a shortcut because your personal story demands it, or if you're really, really desperate, sinking into Duat to find places in an Arisen's memory and idle dreams.<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in that last one especially, because given nonlinear time and the fiends, it's the most like the venerable Warhammer Warp. There's even inhuman gods waiting there to throw obstacles in your path, or find vulnerable people to mark benbenet and bring their will to the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:17:06-08:00","id":1351503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1342225#post1342225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've semi-jokingly noted, but something I think would be neat to see is that if there are any actual aliens humans run into (rather than simply having different splats be the 'aliens' of sorts), they'd see humans as the unspeakable horror of the universe. Why? Because humanity is so <i>changing</i> so gosh dang much. They can be turned into blood drinking vampires, their children can be born with their &quot;souls&quot; being a mishmash of human and spirits of rage, they can ascend into beings that play with the very fabric of reality, they can become fae wielding the power of their greaters, and so much more stranger and scarier things. Even their <i>dead</i> don't stop changing into strange and mutually exclusive things. Further, while humans aren't the only things on earth that can do this on earth, they tend to be the ones who get changed the most while staying visually the same the most.<br /> <br /> Humans may be scared of what's in outer space, but considering what any one human being could become under any number of circumstances, humanity may be the <i>real</i> horror in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200bTo this, and to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> we can only say:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The oldest and strongest emotion of mankind is </span></span></span><b>fear</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, and the oldest and strongest kind of </span></span></span><b>fear</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is </span></span></span><b>fear of the unknown</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">. (Lovecraft)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">There is much unknown in space....<br /> <br /> Personally it sounds fantastic to present a far-future space setting in which humans can be considered from the perspective of other sentient beings encountering them and fitting them into their own ecology and universe-view. It mirrors what we could imagine the reaction of the creatures of earth might have, to the expansion of humanity and its civilization. <br /> <br /> There is a reason the most common wild animal reaction to man is terror.<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T15:05:27-08:00","id":1351549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1351341#post1351341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm on a kick.<br /> <br /> I think what we really need, along with splat-based ships, is alternate hyperdrives.<br /> <br /> Most people probably use the Void and the Gates to it; it's relatively safe, as most ghosts at worse will stow away to get back to a living world to resolve their anchors, and the Underworld is already partly a sea that can be conceptualized and navigated as such. But sometimes, you want speed, or an unexpected route, or flexibility in where you enter/exit hyperspace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made brief mention of this in a recent thread dedicated to sci-fi in the OG World of Darkness, but I can\u2019t get the idea out of my head of a vampire ship that predates faster than light travel, just pootling along and taking however long it needs to take in order to find fresh blood because the crew is immortal and can wait out the trip with their native ability to sleep away the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 11-28-2019, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:02:15-08:00","id":1351574,"title":"","content":"Dead Space and Death Stranding are really giving me vibes of doing stuff like the Gate Drives and the Chiral Networks to mess around with the Ocean of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T18:35:06-08:00","id":1355100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go#post1342129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> explore the role of the God-Machine in the wider cosmos (we already know about the relay in Sirius)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, uh...what's this, now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T19:51:00-08:00","id":1355110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1355100#post1355100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, uh...what's this, now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh\u2026 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sopdet\" target=\"_blank\">pay no attention to the ancient Egyptian goddess behind the veil</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T20:30:13-08:00","id":1355751,"title":"","content":"Oh my god yes, I have wanted more space stuff for the world of darkness since I first learned about the original Infinite Macabre.<br /> <br /> The thing I'd want most out of it would be more detailed systems and discussion about creating alien species and civilizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T23:02:29-08:00","id":1355780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enderdragon1201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1355751#post1355751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god yes, I have wanted more space stuff for the world of darkness since I first learned about the original Infinite Macabre.<br /> <br /> The thing I'd want most out of it would be more detailed systems and discussion about creating alien species and civilizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little cautious on this. Science fiction usually demands a set of rules for what is and what is not allowed. Violating those rules can then seem like a cheat. In contrast the CoD are more steeped in horror and mystery. Putting them in an sf setting might demand removing a lot of that mystery. It would be sad if vampires just became another type of alien, and prometheans just another type of robot.<br /> <br /> As a geezer I remember the heyday of a TV show called the X-Files. In the same fictional universe there were Angels, the absolute agents of the Judeo-Christian divine, put in the same world with an alien &quot;black-oil&quot; nano-virus that could take control of people and even turn them into a chrysalis for a space alien. I always wondered how the series would handle the two encountering one another. Given the track record of the writing, the answer would probably not have been pretty. <br /> <br /> One RPG that sort of does this well is the Warhammer 40k universe. There are spaceships and demons co-existing. However it works in part because no-one really understands science anymore in that universe and so the supernatural is never truly subjected to scientific analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T01:03:55-08:00","id":1357326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1342129-infinite-macabre-to-darkly-go?p=1355780#post1355780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little cautious on this. Science fiction usually demands a set of rules for what is and what is not allowed. Violating those rules can then seem like a cheat. In contrast the CoD are more steeped in horror and mystery. Putting them in an sf setting might demand removing a lot of that mystery. It would be sad if vampires just became another type of alien, and prometheans just another type of robot.<br /> <br /> As a geezer I remember the heyday of a TV show called the X-Files. In the same fictional universe there were Angels, the absolute agents of the Judeo-Christian divine, put in the same world with an alien &amp;quot;black-oil&amp;quot; nano-virus that could take control of people and even turn them into a chrysalis for a space alien. I always wondered how the series would handle the two encountering one another. Given the track record of the writing, the answer would probably not have been pretty. <br /> <br /> One RPG that sort of does this well is the Warhammer 40k universe. There are spaceships and demons co-existing. However it works in part because no-one really understands science anymore in that universe and so the supernatural is never truly subjected to scientific analysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, what I want is not at all to make the already existing supernatural stuff into aliens and technology, I want systems and discussions for making your own aliens. Discussions about how to design systems for custom techonology could also be quite interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T22:34:16-07:00","id":1446914,"title":"","content":"&quot;A ship\u2019s Acceleration is five times the Speed rating. This is measured in miles-per-turn (which, if you care, means that a ship with Speed five moves at about twenty-five miles per turn or eight miles per second, and the speed of light is about fifty miles per second).&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bthis is wrong. speed of light is almost 200k miles per second. page 8, bottom left paragraph<br /> <br /> if this book gets redone. I hope they fix this mistake","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}